./mike/kb/archive/[REDACTED]-nightly.md:154:- [[REDACTED]4:00:48Z] quant-skeptic/verification — ❌ REFUTED VERIFY: oshares-live-wire-viecA-viecB-va-loi-vendor-AIS: {"finding_topic": "oshares-live-wire-viecA-viecB-va-loi-vendor-AIS", "verdict": "REFUTED", "confidence": "high", "checks": {"look_ahead_leak": "fail — anchor selection IS point-in-time (verified: 2020-05-05 anchors to the 2020-04-06 AIS, not a later row; A5 passes; _suspect_ais filters effective_date/exright_date <= asof). BUT the `_sane` gate decides whether to ACCEPT a PIT value by comparing it to the RESTATED ticker_financial.OShares at that exec date (oshares_pit.py:206-211, called at :247) — a future-contaminated number used as an in-backtest decision input at 412/7610 cells, and it is the gate the report credits with killing the +0,94pp. Separately, 916 fallback + 412 gated cells retain the restated look-ahead by design (disclosed).", "oos_robustness": "na — a data-plumbing wire, not an alpha claim; no IS/OOS split is meaningful. Per-year table exists and the 12,44/12,45 delta is inside noise in every year.", "panel_curation_bias": "pass — universe is a live ticker_prune-derived pull with fa_ratings_8l<=3 gate, top-60 liquidity pool, top-30 by rule; zero hardcoded names. 12,45% CAGR is far below the ~25,7% auditable ceiling; no >30%-from-2014 claim anywhere.", "reproducibility_selfcheck": "pass — best reproducibility I have seen from this fleet. I re-ran oshares_pit selfcheck (37/37 PASS), [REDACTED]_core_select_audit.py end-to-end (liq 12.45%/0.65/-46.6%, core0.5 12.14%, core1.0 14.51%, 6691/7610 live, 412 blocked, 1132 moved, nav_recon_err 0.00 VND x3, SPOTCHECK 5/5 — every figure matches), and diffed /tmp/r8l_off vs data/ myself: exactly 1 cell of 39x771=30.069, KHP sales_yield 13.9351->13.928 (-0,051%), rating 771/771, three CSVs byte-identical.", "param_overfit": "fail — SANITY_FACTOR=3,0 is unswept and load-bearing: it alone accounts for essentially the whole -0,95pp correction (13,38 -> 12,43). Author states plainly it is an argument, not a measurement (residual risk #3). Mitigating: two independent gate designs land at 12,43 and 12,45, which is plateau-like evidence for the correction itself. EXPLAIN_TOL=0,001 was separately verified as a real plateau [1e-4, 0,08] in a prior round and is imported, not re-declared.", "capacity_adv_realism": "na — no capital deployment changes. Viec A is an audit/R&D script (nothing re-pinned, R3/custom_basket.py untouched); Viec B is behaviourally neutral and its basket is the top-30 liquidity names.", "arithmetic_mechanism": "fail — the shipped invariant 'net effect can only be to remove look-ahead, never to introduce a new gap' / 'strictly better than status quo' (oshares_pit.py:233-234) is false. Reproduced: FPT at exec date 2020-05-05 returns 461.723.054 (AIS_EXACT, reason PIT) vs the pre-wire 681.668.102; truth is 681.668.102, confirmed by two independent sources (two consecutive quarterly rows, and the next AIS 783.987.486 = 681.668.102 x 1,15 to 0,0088% after the 2020-05-13 15% stock dividend). Error -32,3%, ungated: ratio 0,677 is inside x3, and _suspect_ais skips the pair because the intervening zero-ratio ESOP is a _roll blocker -> `continue` (:195-196). Mirror problem: IDC suspects = ['2020-05-28','2022-09-05'] — the CORRECT 2022-09-05 AIS is flagged purely because its predecessor is the bad row. Consequence: the 1.132 changed cells are a mixture of look-ahead removed + new errors introduced + 412 cells reverted onto look-ahead, so 'khu look-ahead doi 14,9% o nhung KHONG doi loi nhuan => custom_basket.py khong gap phai re-pin' does not follow. Counts and coverage arithmetic itself all check out (6691+916+3=7610; 1132/7610=14,87%; 39x771=30.069)."}, "independent_recompute": "Four independent re[REDACTED]s, all from my own session: (1) [REDACTED]_core_select_audit.py re-run end-to-end — liq 12.45%/Sharpe 0.65/MaxDD -46.6%, core0.5 12.14%, core1.0 14.51%, coverage 6691/7610 (87.9%), 916 fallback, 3 none, 1132 mcap cells moved (14.9%), 412 gate-blocked over 54 tickers, nav_recon_err 0.00 VND on all three variants, SPOTCHECK 5/5 — every published figure matched exactly. (2) rating_8l A/B: my own pandas cell-by-cell diff of /tmp/r8l_off vs data/ returned exactly 1 differing cell (KHP sales_yield 13.9351 -> 13.928, rel -0.0509%), rating identical 771/771, top30/buynow/screener byte-identical via cmp. (3) oshares_pit selfcheck 37/37 PASS. (4) Fresh BQ pulls of tav2_bq.corporate_action confirmed the IDC and AAA vendor errors to the share, and the full-table AIS invariant sieve reproduced in the same ballpark (2.852 pairs / 68,4% exact / 100 gross / 68 tickers raw, vs 2.807 / 69,4% / 110 / 74 claimed; the >2x arm matched exactly at 40). The refutation itself is also a re[REDACTED]: oshares_pit(['FPT'],'2020-05-05',{'FPT':681668102}) returns 461.723.054 from oshares_live at AIS_EXACT.", "killer_objection": "The wire can make a number WORSE, not merely less look-ahead: at the real 2020-05-05 rebalance it swaps FPT's correct 681.668.102 for 461.723.054 (-32,3%) at the highest-confidence label AIS_EXACT, because the vendor interleaves two AIS series and the invariant gate skips exactly that pair (intervening zero-ratio ESOP is a _roll blocker -> `continue`) while the x3 magnitude gate sees a harmless 0,677 ratio. So the 14,9% of moved cells is a mixture of look-ahead removed and fresh errors injected, and the '±0,01pp therefore the look-ahead is harmless, custom_basket.py needs no re-pin' inference is not supported by this experiment.", "recommended_reruns": ["Quantify the mixture before drawing any conclusion from the ±0,01pp: count exec-date cells where |live/quarterly - 1| > 10% AND the cell was NOT gated, hand-check a stratified sample of them, and report look-ahead-removed vs error-injected separately.", "Close the FPT hole in _suspect_ais: an AIS whose shares_total_after cannot be reconciled with the previous AIS *because a _roll blocker sits between them* is UNVERIFIABLE, not verified — it must decline (or fall back), not be served at AIS_EXACT. Today line 195-196 `continue`s and the row is accepted unconditionally.", "Delete or correct the 'Strictly better than status quo / can only remove look-ahead, never introduce a new gap' invariant in oshares_pit.py:25-26 and :233-234 and the same sentence in the report — a false invariant in a docstring is what the next consumer will trust.", "Add the under-flagging direction to RUI_RO_TON_DU: the current list frames gate error as safe-only ('rơi về hành vi hôm nay'), which is true for false positives and false for false negatives.", "Sweep SANITY_FACTOR over [1,5 .. 10] and publish the CAGR / blocked-cell curve; a threshold carrying ~0,95pp of a measured correction cannot stay an argument.", "Investigate whether the FPT-style interleaved AIS series is separable at source (issue_method_name_vi / event_description_vi / organ_code) so it can be filtered categorically rather than by magnitude — and fold this case, not just IDC/AAA, into the recommended oshares_live-internal patch round.", "Update oshares_live.py's header, which still reads 'STATUS: NOT WIRED. No consumer may read this module until a second quant-skeptic pass clears it' while this commit wires two consumers (the round-2 [REDACTED]D/medium of [REDACTED]T06:06:49Z exists on the bus, but the file's own gate was never lifted).", "Viec B needs no rerun — leave OSHARES_RECONCILE=1 and keep collecting the burn-in log."], "summary": "This is careful, honest, well-instrumented work and almost all of it reproduced exactly in my own session — the 37/37 selfcheck, all three backtest variants to the digit with 0,00 VND NAV identity, the one-cell rating_8l diff, and both hand-checked vendor errors straight from BigQuery. Viec B (the live leg) survives every attack and is structurally immune to the defect below, because oshares_reconciled only accepts a live value within 0,1% of the quarterly one and a -32% error can never pass that. Viec A is what fails. The module ships an invariant — 'the net effect can only be to remove look-ahead, never to introduce a new gap', 'strictly better than status quo' — that I broke with a reproducible counterexample at a real rebalance date: FPT on 2020-05-05 gets 461.723.054 instead of the correct 681.668.102 (-32,3%), served at the highest-confidence label AIS_EXACT, because the vendor interleaves two AIS series and neither gate covers that shape (the invariant gate skips the pair on a _roll blocker; the x3 gate sees a benign 0,677 ratio). Two independent sources pin the true count. The same gate design also flags IDC's CORRECT 2022-09-05 row merely for sitting next to the bad one, so the flag set is 'transitions adjacent to an anomaly', not 'vendor errors'. Consequently the 14,9% of moved mcap cells is a mixture of look-ahead removed, errors injected, and cells reverted onto look-ahead, and the report's headline inference — that the ±0,01pp shows this look-ahead is harmless and custom_basket.py need not be re-pinned — is not established by the experiment as run. REFUTED on Viec A's stated invariant and the conclusion drawn from it; Viec B stands and I would not hold it up."}
./mike/kb/archive/[REDACTED]-nightly.md:171:- [[REDACTED]6:24:45Z] quant-skeptic/verification — ✅ [REDACTED]VERIFY: oshares-vong4-doi-cong-chung-nhan-AIS-vao-oshares_live: {"finding_topic": "oshares-vong4-doi-cong-chung-nhan-AIS-vao-oshares_live", "verdict": "[REDACTED]D", "confidence": "high", "checks": {"look_ahead_leak": "pass — no forward column touched (`profit_*`/`O*`/`Pattern_*` absent from oshares_live.py and oshares_pit.py). PIT discipline verified in code and by test: `_ais_verdicts` filters AIS by `effective_date <= asof` and ISS by `exright_date <= asof` (oshares_live.py:389-393), so a 2026 AIS cannot retro-refute a 2019 answer — asserted by N8 (oshares_live) and A5 (oshares_pit), both PASS on my run. The verdict for anchor A depends only on the AIS immediately BEFORE A, never after. Cache breadth is irrelevant: ab_snapshot builds one cache at UNTIL=[REDACTED] and queries back to 2016, and the per-date outputs still matched byte-for-byte.", "oos_robustness": "na — this is a data-integrity gate on a vendor feed, not a return claim. Nearest analogue was run anyway: the A/B basket spans 2016→2026 (8 dates) and consumer A spans 2014→2026 (48 rebal dates × 171 names = 7,610 cells) with per-year output printed; the certification gate's behaviour is stable across the whole span, and the only quoted CAGR (liq 12.44%) is a control number that must NOT move, and did not.", "panel_curation_bias": "pass — the 20-name A/B basket is adversarially constructed, not cherry-picked favourably: it is deliberately enriched with the three known-broken names (IDC/AAA/FPT) plus clean controls (VNM/TCB), a no-AIS name (DHG), a same-day-double-event name (MBB) and an ISS-blocked name (HAH). Independent of it, consumer A ran the full un-curated [REDACTED] universe (7,610 cells) and consumer B the full 771-name rating universe from a live BQ pull — 0 changes in B, exact control re[REDACTED] in A.", "reproducibility_selfcheck": "pass — I re-ran all four selfchecks myself: oshares_live 32/32, oshares_pit 48/48, oshares_wire 11/11, corp_action_daily 127/127 (the last including TZ1/TZ2 under `env -u TZ` and a foreign TZ). Consumer A printed `nav_recon_err=0.00 VND` on all three legs plus SPOTCHECK PASS against BQ prices. Every blocking case has a proof-by-contradiction twin (N3/A6/A11: reopening `_SERVE_AIS_VERDICTS` really does bring back IDC 3,000,000,000 and FPT 461,723,054) AND a negative control (N5/N6/A13a) so the gate cannot pass by blocking everything; fail-closed is tested by making the certifier raise for real (N4/A13). snap_before.json verified genuinely pre-change.", "param_overfit": "pass — only one judgment knob was introduced this round, `_SERVE_AIS_VERDICTS`, and its sensitivity is measured, not argued: serving NO_PRIOR gives live 6,603 (86.8%) / liq CAGR 12.44%, excluding it gives 6,290 (82.7%) / 12.46% — 4.1pp of coverage traded for 0.02pp of CAGR, i.e. inside noise, so the choice is not perched on a peak. `EXPLAIN_TOL=0.1%` and `SANITY_FACTOR` are inherited from rounds 2-3 (already swept), not re-tuned here. Rollback is a one-word edit with the reverted behaviour explicitly re-measured.", "capacity_adv_realism": "na — no sizing, ADV, or order path touched. The only number that reaches a traded decision is `OShares` feeding `ps` in rating_8l's composite, and consumer B measured 0/771 changes there.", "arithmetic_mechanism": "pass on every number I could recompute, BUT the consumer-C impact figure is understated. Reproduced exactly: 160-cell A/B (0 contract diffs, 18 raw diffs all number→None), liq 12.44%/6603/500, EVF and SHB arithmetic from BQ to the digit (EVF expect 762,686,029 vs actual 704,248,289, quarterly frozen at 760,565,802 through [REDACTED]; SHB (b)=4,191,361,564 vs actual 4,594,200,024; old value +0.6294% off quarterly). Mechanism is consistent: gate placed AFTER computation so the `blockers`/UNKNOWN_RATIO branch keeps precedence, which is exactly why the pit-layer blocked set is unchanged. Design decision 3 verified: AIS_EXACT and AIS_UNCERTIFIED are both outside `_DECLINED` and `summarize()` buckets on the unchanged 'KHÔNG XÁC MINH ĐƯỢC' reason prefix, so no row moves between columns of the burn-in CSV. The understatement: 'tác động 2/33' was measured at only 1 of 3 `oshares_at` call sites — see killer_objection.", "look_ahead_leak_note": "n/a"}, "independent_recompute": "Four independent re[REDACTED]s, all matched to quoted precision. (1) Re-ran `ab_snapshot.py` from scratch — 160/160 cells byte-identical to the committed `snap_after.json`; diffing against `snap_before.json` gave exactly 0 contract-field diffs, 0 reason diffs, and 18 raw diffs of which 18 were number→None and 0 were number→different-number. (2) Re-ran `[REDACTED]_core_select_audit.py` end to end — liq CAGR 12.44%, live=6603 (86.8%), fallback=1004, none=3, gate blocked 500 cells, `nav_recon_err=0.00 VND` on all three legs, SELF-CHECK PASS | SPOTCHECK PASS. (3) Re-ran all four selfchecks (32/32, 48/48, 11/11, 127/127). (4) Queried `tav2_bq.corporate_action` and `tav2_bq.ticker_financial` directly for EVF and SHB and reconstructed both certification failures by hand — every figure in the 'Cái giá' table is exact, and I additionally established that SHB's rejected anchor (AIS 2025-10-07 = 4,594,200,024) is corroborated to +0.011% by quarterly 2025-10-23 (4,593,703,838), i.e. the false alarm is caused by the broken PRIOR row 2025-08-11, confirming the report's own 'báo oan có thật' reading.", "killer_objection": "The consumer-C impact statement is measured at only one of three `oshares_at` call sites, and the real number is 3 tickers, not 2. `consumer_c_driver.py` reproduces only `corp_action_daily.py:1008` (`cur = oshares_at(track, asof)`). I ran the other two call sites with the gate on vs off: `crosscheck()` (line 872, evaluated at each ticker's QUARTERLY date, not asof) flips EVF, SHB **and TCB** from `DIVERGENT` to `NO_MODEL_VALUE` — TCB is a live held position in both accounts and is nowhere in the report; `check_retro()` (line 837) additionally drops EVF/SHB from retro comparison. Knock-on: the daily Discord alert at line 1182 formats these as `(d['oshares_live'] or 0)` with `err_pct` defaulting to 0, so tomorrow's operator message will read \"TCB@... corp-action 0 vs bq_admin 7,086,... (0.00%)\" — a declined answer rendered as perfect agreement on a held name. The formatting flaw pre-dates round 4 (NO_MODEL_VALUE was already reachable via UNKNOWN_RATIO/NO_ANCHOR, and is selfchecked at corp_action_daily_selfcheck.py:299), but round 4 is what makes it fire on three held tickers that previously printed real numbers. None of this voids the headline — no number served to trading changed, the gate direction stays conservative, and the A/B/consumer-A/consumer-B re[REDACTED]s are exact — but the report's own stated purpose for that section ('đừng đọc 0-diff thành không mất gì') is defeated by an impact count that is itself incomplete.", "recommended_reruns": ["Extend `consumer_c_driver.py` to all THREE `oshares_at` call sites in corp_action_daily.py (lines 837 check_retro, 872 crosscheck, 1008 cur) and re-publish the impact line as '3/33 mã (EVF, SHB, TCB) — 2 tại điểm publish, 3 tại điểm đối soát chéo'; the crosscheck site evaluates at the quarterly date, a different asof, so it cannot be inferred from the asof-only measurement.", "Fix the misleading Discord render at corp_action_daily.py:1182 — NO_MODEL_VALUE rows must print 'mô hình TỪ CHỐI trả số (<method>)' instead of falling through `or 0` to 'corp-action 0 ... (0.00%)'. Add a selfcheck case that asserts the rendered string for a NO_MODEL_VALUE row, since the existing case only asserts the dict field is None.", "Add a monitoring backstop for the disclosed invariant-coverage loss: track the count of tickers with value=None in the published snapshot per day and alert if it grows, so fail-closed silence does not become permanent unmonitored silence (the report flags this as 'cái giá' but leaves no detector).", "Answer the open item explicitly rather than leaving it hanging: measure whether SANITY_FACTOR's magnitude layer is needed for direct `oshares_at` callers (corp_action_daily has no such layer), e.g. by replaying the ~27 gross-error cells the certification gate does not catch through the direct-call path."], "summary": "This is a genuine refactor and it holds up. The AIS certification gate really did move into `oshares_at`, direct calls really are gated now, and I independently reproduced every headline number to the quoted precision: 160/160 A/B cells identical to the committed post-change snapshot, 0 contract-field diffs against a snapshot I verified is genuinely pre-change, 18 direct-call cells changed with all 18 being number→None and none becoming a different number, consumer A's liq CAGR 12.44% with nav_recon_err 0.00 VND, consumer B 0/771 changed, and all four selfchecks passing on my own run including under stripped and foreign TZ. The BQ arithmetic behind the disclosed EVF/SHB cost is exact, and I independently confirmed SHB is a true false alarm caused by a broken prior row rather than a broken anchor. Point-in-time discipline is intact by construction and by test. The one real defect I found is a completeness failure, not a correctness one: `consumer_c_driver.py` measured only one of three `oshares_at` call sites in the live cron, so the reported '2/33 mã' is actually 3 tickers once `crosscheck()` is included — TCB, a live held position in both accounts, silently moves from DIVERGENT to NO_MODEL_VALUE and will render in tomorrow's Discord alert as 'corp-action 0 ... (0.00%)' through a pre-existing `or 0` formatting flaw. That degrades a monitoring report on a held name and contradicts the report's own insistence that the cost be stated honestly, but it does not change any number served to trading and does not void the headline. [REDACTED]D, with the consumer-C impact statement to be corrected to 3 tickers and the alert render fixed before this round is called closed."}
