mike/kb/archive/[REDACTED]-nightly.md:43:- [[REDACTED]T04:58:10Z] quant-skeptic/verification — ❌ REFUTED VERIFY: viec-A-B-corporate-action-oshares-live-va-vendor-validation: {"finding_topic": "viec-A-B-corporate-action-oshares-live-va-vendor-validation", "verdict": "REFUTED", "confidence": "high", "checks": {"look_ahead_leak": "fail — `ticker_financial.OShares` is restated, not point-in-time. 631 rows / 247 tickers since 2024 carry an OShares exactly equal to a shares_total_after whose AIS effective_date is strictly later (avg 140d, max 819d); 146 of those predate even the driving ISS ex-right date, so the count was unknowable to anyone. `oshares_at()` consumes these as facts available at `asof`. Measured: HAH 2026-03-01 and 2026-05-20 return 185.840.401 vs true listed 168.861.212 = +10,06%, emitted as `ANCHOR_ONLY` with no warning. The FPT 2025-07-22 row cited as proof that 'ticker_financial đôi khi nhanh hơn hẳn' is itself a member of that restated set (matches AIS eff 2025-09-12 exactly), so the stated justification for anchor-by-date cannot be distinguished from the artifact.", "oos_robustness": "na — no return/alpha claim; IS/OOS split does not apply to a share-count reconstruction.", "panel_curation_bias": "fail — Việc B's entire validation is one hand-picked ticker (FPT) plus an all-event-free control leg (DHG/PVT/TCB/ACB/HDB). FPT's ESOP tranches fall in the 30% minority carrying a nonzero exercise_ratio, so no case in the suite exercises the 75% zero-ratio class the method actually breaks on. Việc A is separately limited by the author's own disclosed n=6, one month, cash-only — correctly disclosed, not hidden.", "reproducibility_selfcheck": "pass — reran all three live: corp_action_lib 7/7 PASS, oshares_live all PASS, dividend_adjusted_return 58 PASS / 0 FAIL. Freshness triple reproduced exactly (max_ingested [REDACTED] 15:48:52, n_days=1, max_public [REDACTED], n=36.149). Note: payload claims oshares_live '11/11'; the file emits 12 checks (1,2,3,3b,4,5,6,7,8,8b,8c,9), all PASS — undercount, not overclaim.", "param_overfit": "na — no tuned numeric parameter; the anchor tie-break and _dedup_iss key are design choices, not fitted values.", "capacity_adv_realism": "na — not a tradeable-edge claim.", "arithmetic_mechanism": "fail — the stated mechanism ('Oshares phải đếm MỌI ISS') is not what the code does. Roll-forward is `value *= (1 + exercise_ratio)`, and 667/884 executed non-accruing ISS since 2020 carry exercise_ratio = 0.0 (+18 NULL): private placement 303/399, ESOP 260/371, convertible 58/62, auction 30/33, merger 13/16, bondholder 3/3 — vs 0/1.683 among price-adjusting ISS. Multiplying by 1.0 is a no-op, so the class the discovery says must be counted is precisely the class that cannot be. Real cases: HAH 2025-03-20 convertible +8.551.327 CP (+7,05%) at ratio 0,0; HAH 2026-03-12 convertible ~+14,5tr (+8,6%) at ratio 0,0. Compounding: a zero-ratio event still flips `method` to `ISS_ESTIMATE`, asserting an adjustment that did not occur. Separately, HAH ESOP ex [REDACTED] ratio 0,01858 vs implied 6.000.000/185.840.401 = 3,229% (1,74×); payload misdates that event to 2025-07-28 (docstring is correct at [REDACTED]). Việc A's arithmetic is sound and the trust hierarchy is genuinely not inverted (`cash_per_share` at line 191 releases only CASH_[REDACTED]D).", "extra_note": "Việc A, the taxonomy statement, the freshness warning and the bq --max_rows fix all PASS independently — the REFUTED verdict is scoped to Việc B (oshares_live.py)."}, "independent_recompute": "Yes, four separate re[REDACTED]s. (1) Re-ran all three selfchecks live: 7/7, 12/12, 58/58 PASS. (2) Re-queried corporate_action freshness — MAX(ingested_at)=[REDACTED] 15:48:52, n_ingest_days=1, MAX(public_date)=[REDACTED], n=36.149, matching the report exactly. (3) Re-queried all six vendor DIV values from BQ — MBB 1.000, BID 450, CTG 450, VCB 450, NCT 8.000, SAB 3.000, all event_status='executed', matching the 6/6 table to the dong including the CTG+VCB same-ex-date pair. (4) Independently reconstructed HAH's true listed share count from AIS.shares_total_after and compared against oshares_at() — exposed a +10,055% error at 2026-03-01 and 2026-05-20 that the model reports as ANCHOR_ONLY. Also ran two BQ aggregates the finding never ran: the 631-row/247-ticker restatement scan (146 hard look-ahead) and the exercise_ratio=0.0 census by issue method.", "killer_objection": "Việc B's core design choice and its core discovery break each other. The anchor is chosen by date because ticker_financial is 'sometimes faster' — but ticker_financial.OShares is restated, so 'faster' is mostly an artifact (631 rows carry a strictly-later AIS count; 146 predate the ex-right itself), and the roll-forward that is supposed to bridge the remaining gap silently multiplies by 1.0 on 75% of the non-accruing ISS the discovery says must be counted. The 12/12 PASS is not evidence against this: no ticker in the test suite has a zero-ratio event, and the one 'must-pass' case (FPT) is a name where both defects happen to be inert. A suite built from cases where the method works cannot detect a class of case where it fails by +10%.", "recommended_reruns": ["BLOCK oshares_live.py from any consumer (rating_8l, market cap, EPS) until both defects are fixed — this is stronger than the report's own §6.4 'cần đối soát rộng hơn 1 mã': the failure is by event class, not by sample size.", "Add a TRAP entry to mike/kb/data_registry/ for ticker_financial.OShares recording that it is RESTATED, not point-in-time (631 rows / 247 tickers / max 819 days early since 2024, 146 hard look-ahead) — per coding_guidelines §9 this must exist before any new code reads the column.", "Redesign the anchor rule: treat AIS.shares_total_after as the only authoritative anchor, and admit a ticker_financial row only when it does NOT equal a later AIS count (i.e. run the 631-row test as a live gate, not a one-off audit).", "Replace ratio-based roll-forward with shares_delta where present