mike/kb/archive/[REDACTED]-nightly.md:66:- [[REDACTED]T06:06:49Z] quant-skeptic/verification — ✅ [REDACTED]VERIFY: viec-B-C-vong-2-da-va-CHO-quant-skeptic-vong-2: {"finding_topic": "viec-B-C-vong-2-da-va-CHO-quant-skeptic-vong-2", "verdict": "[REDACTED]D", "confidence": "medium", "checks": {"look_ahead_leak": "pass — no forward column (profit_2W/1M/2M/3M, O1W..O2Y, *_center_*, Pattern_*_3Y) is touched by any of the 4 scripts. B1 is itself a leak REMOVAL and I reproduced its measurement from my own BQ query exactly: 2667 rows/576 tickers carry an OShares equal (<1cp) to a LATER executed AIS shares_total_after (max lead 2693d); 626/247 since 2024-01-01 (max 819d); 145/75 hard (an ISS goes ex after the quarterly row). New anchor = AIS primary + quarterly row admitted only if self-explaining. _explain_quarterly does read a later AIS but only to REJECT (conservative direction). For C, Close/Price(asof) from today's vintage is correct retrospective total-return accounting on a frozen past entry, not a decision input. Disclosed blind spot (restatement whose backing AIS is not yet ingested) is stated honestly.", "oos_robustness": "na — reporting/data-plumbing correctness, no alpha claim is made. Caveat for citation: the report's +4.49pp / +2.96pp / +0.81pp alphas come from hand-picked 4- and 9-name panels over ~6 weeks, n≈1 episode, and no IS/OOS split is possible or claimed. The converge report does disclose the date-frame mismatch on the vs-[REDACTED] figure.", "panel_curation_bias": "na — no CAGR/universe/>30% claim anywhere; oshares_live is NOT WIRED (confirmed by grep: only a comment in corp_action_lib.py and an unrelated SQL alias 'oshares_live' in update_shares_live.py). The paper books ARE curated panels, which matters only for reading the alpha numbers, not for the arithmetic claims under review.", "reproducibility_selfcheck": "pass — re-ran everything in my own shell: paper_entry_adjust 21/21, oshares_live 22/22, report_return_gate PASS (35 cases), crosscheck T1 13/13 + T2 4/4, real gate run 13/13 OK. Reverse-proof rebuilt from scratch (Close:=Price pre-event vintage parquet) reproduced EXACTLY: 6 fails on 4 positions (alphalens MBB, converge MBB/HAH/CTR), 9/9 no-event positions untouched. HAH ESOP ex-date [REDACTED] r=0.01858 verified and no HAH ISS exists on 2025-07-28 (nearest prior 2025-08-07 stock div 30%). Registry TRAP entry exists with status:TRAP and both links. DEFECT: '+12 ca moi' is +11 by machine count (24->35) — the same hand-typed-count error B4 declares fixed, because the len(ran) fix was not applied to report_return_gate.py.", "param_overfit": "pass — EXPLAIN_TOL=0.001 sits mid-plateau, verified by sweep: every value in [1e-4, 0.08] both rejects HAH 2026-03-01's restated 185,840,401 and accepts FPT 2025-07-22's real early 1,703,507,121. Breaks only below 1e-4 (rejects real early data) and at >=0.11 (swallows the restatement). ~3 orders of magnitude wide, and the threshold is justified from measured gaps (FPT 0.0013% vs HAH +10.06%). VINTAGE_TOL_DAYS=2 vs the real 14-day lag also has wide margin.", "capacity_adv_realism": "na — paper marks with no execution, sizing or ADV assumption. Directionally conservative: accrue-only treats the right as lapsed, so the paper book understates relative to a real cash account.", "arithmetic_mechanism": "pass with one defect — TERP inversion matches to FLOAT EQUALITY, not 6 decimals: 20200/24250 == 25250/30312.5 == 404/485, proving the vendor uses TERP with S=10,000 and r=10%/15%. I re-derived accrue-only independently (lapsed right => entry_adj = P0*adj_cash/(1+r_sd)) and got 0.835955, matching. All portfolio arithmetic reproduces. accrue-vs-dilute taxonomy confirmed on real data (HAH ESOP [REDACTED] produces no ratio step). T1's per-position filter correctly re-narrows exright_date > that position's own asof, so the asof_min query widening creates no false positive. DEFECT: C3's [REDACTED] reach — see killer_objection.", "": ""}, "independent_recompute": "Reproduced 3 headline returns from raw parquet + my own arithmetic (MBB alphalens -2.9245% -> -2.9%; alphalens portfolio +0.8985% / alpha +4.4915pp -> +0.90% / +4.49pp; converge portfolio -1.2450% / alpha +2.9608pp -> -1.24% / +2.96pp) and generated the live report sections, whose printed numbers matched all six including the +0.81pp vs-[REDACTED] figure. Reproduced all 6 B1 counts and all 8 B2 counts from my own BigQuery queries — exact. Rebuilt the reverse-proof independently (6 fails / 4 positions, 9/9 untouched) — exact. Verified EXPLAIN_TOL plateau [1e-4, 0.08] by sweep.", "killer_objection": "C3's gate is unreachable in [REDACTED], so it protects nothing today. paper_entry_gate() runs only via run_gate(report_path), whose sole [REDACTED] caller is send_report_email.py — but the report carrying the paper sections, [REDACTED]eport.py (crontab '0 23 * * 0-4' = 06:00 ICT Mon-Fri), posts directly to Discord via notify_thread.sh:123 and never writes a .md file. No .md anywhere in the repo contains PAPER_MARKERS, and send_plan_report.sh / eod_trading_report.sh reference neither report module. Worse, the payload's stated rationale ('[REDACTED] carries the paper section but no account label IN THE FILENAME, so the old early-exit skipped it entirely') presupposes it is a file traversing the gate — a false premise about the [REDACTED] path. The mechanism is correct and demonstrably blocks in both directions; it simply never runs on the channel where these numbers reach the user. Anyone reading this finding would believe the paper numbers are now gated. They are not.", "recommended_reruns": ["Wire the gate into the channel that actually carries the numbers: have [REDACTED]eport.py either call report_return_gate.paper_entry_gate() on its assembled message before notify_thread.sh (fail-closed, do not post on CHAN), or write a dated .md and route it through send_report_email.py. Until then state plainly in the report that the paper leg is NOT active in [REDACTED].", "Apply B4's own fix to report_return_gate.py: make its selfcheck print a machine-counted total (len(ran)) like the other two files, then correct '+12 ca' to the true +11 in the report and in the af1e201b commit-message narrative.", "Add an ABSOLUTE cache-freshness floor alongside the relative stale_years(): a wholly frozen bq_cache flags nothing today, and the only thing that catches it (T1) lives behind the gate that does not run.", "Before wiring oshares_live.py: broaden the anchor cross-check well beyond HAH/FPT/NAF/DHG (the 145/75 hard-look-ahead population is the natural sampling frame) and re-check MAX(ingested_at) on corporate_action on [REDACTED]14 as the report already schedules.", "When quoting the paper alphas anywhere downstream, carry the n and the panel-curation caveat; +4.49pp / +2.96pp / +0.81pp over ~6 weeks on 4 and 9 hand-picked names is not evidence of edge.", "Optional but worth a line in the docstring: accrue-only assumes the right LAPSES, yet quyen mua is frequently transferable on HOSE and selling it needs no cash account — so accrue-only is the conservative floor, not the only defensible convention. Both numbers are already printed side by side, which is what makes this acceptable."], "summary": "Every measurable claim in this finding reproduced in my own environment, and several reproduced more strongly than claimed — the TERP inversion matches to float equality (404/485), not merely six decimals, and I re-derived the accrue-only factor 0.835955 from first principles rather than accepting it. All 6 B1 look-ahead counts and all 8 B2 fail-closed counts came out exact from my own BigQuery queries; the three headline returns, the reverse-proof (6 fails / 4 positions, 9/9 untouched), the crosscheck (T1 13/13, T2 4/4) and all three selfchecks reproduced exactly. EXPLAIN_TOL=0.001 is a real plateau spanning [1e-4, 0.08], not a tuned point. The arithmetic and the fail-closed behaviours are sound, and the patches do what they say. Two defects: the claimed '+12 new cases' is +11 by machine count — the very hand-typed-count error B4 declares closed, because that fix was never applied to report_return_gate.py; and, materially, the C3 gate cannot fire in [REDACTED], since the only report carrying the paper sections posts straight to Discord from [REDACTED]eport.py and never becomes a file for run_gate() to read. The finding's rationale for C3 rests on a false premise about that data path, and readers would wrongly conclude the paper numbers are now protected. I confirm rather than refute because the finding explicitly declines to claim closure and lists its open items, oshares_live is genuinely unwired, and nothing here sits on the live money path — but confidence is medium, not high, until C3's gate is connected to the channel it was built to guard."}
